From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:42:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kvq-once (report 66 items 2-3): GGML_HIP_KVQ_ONCE=1 reads the
 q4_0 KV once per MTP verify; kvq split knobs

flash_attn_ext_kvq gets an ngroups template parameter. ngroups == 2 (q4_0, D 256, an even number of 16-column Q tiles:
Qwen3.5/3.8 verify of 3-5, 9-10 or 14-16 tokens at GQA 6) runs one block of 2 x 8 warps per 2 adjacent Q tiles: warp w
of group g computes tile 2*blockIdx.x + g over exactly the KV rows warp w of the ngroups == 1 kernel handles, so the
K/V bytes of a block are fetched for both tiles at once (the second K read hits the cache), and every q4_0 block of V
is dequantized once into the transposed LDS tile of the warp pair (group g dequantizes blocks [2g, 2g+2) of its lane's
half row, 36 bytes, 4-byte loads). The pair synchronizes through 4 LDS counters per pair with LDS-only release/acquire
fences (a workgroup fence on all address spaces would also wait for the K/V loads in flight). The KV split is still
computed from the number of 16-column tiles, the per-column KQ/softmax/VKQ arithmetic and the warp combine order are
those of the default kernel: bit-identical output by construction. LDS 53.9 KB, 242 VGPRs, no spills; ngroups == 1 keeps
its arithmetic (D 256: 255 VGPRs, only setup scheduling differs). Default off until the GPU numbers are in.

GGML_HIP_KVQ_BLOCKS_PER_SM=N (blocks per SM for the split, every KV type) and GGML_HIP_KVQ_MIN_SPLIT=T (at least T KV
rows per split) are sweep knobs; unset = the old split. Other split points change the order of the sums (KLD gate).

test-backend-ops: q4_0 GQA 6 eval cases with nb 10 and 16 (4 and 6 tiles), perf cases at kv 196608.
